{"state": "Goa", "_meta": {"as_of": "2026-09-25", "districts_note": "Goa has THREE districts since Notification No. 16/29/1/2023-Rev-I/3259 (Revenue Dept, 31-12-2025): North Goa (HQ Panaji: Pernem, Bardez, Tiswadi, Bicholim, Sattari), South Goa (HQ Margao: Ponda, Salcete, Mormugao) and Kushavati (HQ Quepem: Quepem, Sanguem, Dharbandora, Canacona). Source PDF: https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s396b9bff013acedfb1d140579e2fbeb63/uploads/2026/05/17787404111914.pdf (linked from kushavati.goa.gov.in). Ponda taluka is in SOUTH Goa (moved from North Goa in Jan 2015 per the Wikipedia Ponda taluka article and southgoa.nic.in; the 31 Dec 2025 Kushavati notification also lists it under South Goa), not North Goa as in Census 2011 and older boundary files. The 2022 election district grouping still listed its seats under North Goa.", "coordinates_note": "Taluka and district centroids are area centroids computed (EPSG:32643) from DataMeet Goa village polygons (github.com/datameet/indian_village_boundaries/ga, ODbL, Census 2001 village frame), with Dharbandora = its 16 notified villages. Town points: Wikipedia article coordinates where available (replaced by the DataMeet polygon centroid only when the Wikipedia value is 2-decimal and >3 km from the matching polygon), else the DataMeet polygon centroid; null when neither was verifiable. Some Wikipedia coordinates are only 2-decimal precision (~1 km).", "devanagari_note": "Devanagari aliases come from the titles of the linked Marathi (mr) and Konkani (gom) Wikipedia articles for each place; some are Marathi forms (e.g. डिचोली for Bicholim) and some Konkani (e.g. दिवचल).", "villages_note": "villages_and_localities = all Census 2011 census towns (CT) not already in towns[] plus the most populous Census 2011 villages, up to 150 entries. Taluka from the Census 2011 DCHB village/town directory (catalog 368), Dharbandora re-assigned per the 2025 notification; district = current district. lat/lng (where present) = DataMeet village-polygon centroid.