ME gives no source or delimitation info", "notes": "Checked 2026-09-25: HTTP 200, 65 KB, EPSG:4326, 41 features = ACs 1-40 plus one AC_NO=0 / AC_NAME=null polygon (~17 km2, centroid 15.516N 73.865E, Mandovi estuary / Chorao area) that should be dropped. Properties: AC_NO (string \"1\"..\"40\"), AC_NAME (e.g. \"Pernem (SC)\", \"Vasco-Da-Gama\", \"St. Cruz\", \"St. Andre\"), PC_NO (1/2), PC_NAME (\"NORTH GOA\"/\"SOUTH GOA\"), PC_ID (3001/3002), DIST_NAME, DT_CODE, ST_CODE=30, ST_NAME=\"GOA\". POST-2008 delimitation (current 40 AC names incl. Mandrem, Porvorim, Saligao, St. Andre, Fatorda, Nuvem, Velim, Sanvordem; PCs named North/South Goa). Geometry has the same area (3,623.34 km2) as the DataMeet India_AC layer, i.e. the same ECI polling-station-site derived boundaries. DIST_NAME uses the old 2-district assignment (Ponda, Siroda, Marcaim ACs labelled NORTH GOA; no Kushavati). Anjediva island not covered."}, {"what": "AC boundaries (all-India shapefile, filter ST_NAME == GOA)", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/assembly-constituencies/India_AC.shp", "alt_urls": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/assembly-constituencies/India_AC.dbf", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/assembly-constituencies/India_AC.shx", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/assembly-constituencies/India_AC.prj"], "license": "CC BY 2.5 India (per assembly-constituencies/README.md)", "notes": "Checked 2026-09-25: all four files HTTP 200 (shp 6.3 MB). EPSG:4326. Goa = 41 rows (ST_CODE 30): the same 40 ACs + AC_NO 0 as above. Fields: OBJECTID, ST_CODE, ST_NAME, DT_CODE, DIST_NAME, AC_NO (int), AC_NAME, PC_NO, PC_NAME, PC_ID, STATUS, Shape_Leng, Shape_Area. STATUS is null for Goa (the README flags pre-delimitation boundaries only for J&K, Jharkhand, Assam, Manipur, Nagaland and Arunachal). Convert with: ogr2ogr -f GeoJSON -where \"ST_NAME='GOA' AND AC_NO>0\" goa_ac.geojson India_AC.shp. The README warns of some positional shift and some wrong names."}, {"what": "District boundaries (Goa, 2 districts, GeoJSON)", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HindustanTimesLabs/shapefiles/master/state_ut/goa/district/goa_district.json", "license": "MIT (repository licence)", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200, 23 KB, 2 features, properties district (\"North Goa\"/\"South Goa\"), dt_cen_cd, st_cen_cd, st_nm, censuscode (585/586), cartodb_id. Census 2011 districts. PREDATES KUSHAVATI (31-12-2025) and the 2015 move of Ponda to South Goa, so it does not match current districts. To build the current 3 districts, dissolve the DataMeet village layer below."}, {"what": "District boundaries (Goa, alternative GeoJSON)", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/udit-001/india-maps-data/main/geojson/states/goa.geojson", "license": "No licence declared in the repository (github.com/udit-001/india-maps-data); check before redistribution", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200, 2 features, properties dt_code (585/586), district, st_code, year (\"2011_c\"), st_nm. Census 2011 districts; predates Kushavati."}, {"what": "District boundaries (all-India Census 2011 shapefile)", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/Districts/Census_2011/2011_Dist.shp", "alt_urls": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/Districts/Census_2011/2011_Dist.dbf", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/Districts/Census_2011/2011_Dist.shx", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/Districts/Census_2011/2011_Dist.prj"], "license": "CC BY 4.0 (datameet/maps README default)", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200. Fields DISTRICT, ST_NM, ST_CEN_CD, DT_CEN_CD, censuscode; Goa rows North Goa (585) and South Goa (586). Predates Kushavati."}, {"what": "Village boundaries (Goa, GeoJSON); use to derive taluka and current 3-district polygons", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/indian_village_boundaries/master/ga/ga.geojson", "license": "ODbL (datameet/indian_village_boundaries README)", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200, 1.2 MB, 402 polygons (358 villages, 44 towns). Properties NAME, TYPE (Village/Town), SUB_DIST (11 Census talukas, Sattari spelled \"Satari\"), DISTRICT (2 districts), STATE, CEN_2001. Census 2001 frame. Dharbandora is not a SUB_DIST: take the 16 villages Aglote, Bandoli, Camarconda, Caranzol, Codli, Colem, Cormonem, Darbandora, Moissal, Molem, Piliem, Sancordem, Sangod, Sigao, Sonauli and Surla from SUB_DIST Sanguem. Then dissolve: North Goa = Pernem+Bardez+Tiswadi+Bicholim+Satari; South Goa = Ponda+Salcete+Mormugao; Kushavati = Quepem+Sanguem+Dharbandora+Canacona. The district and taluka centroids in this file were computed this way."}, {"what": "State outline", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/States/Admin2.shp", "alt_urls": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/States/Admin2.dbf", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/States/Admin2.shx", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datameet/maps/master/States/Admin2.prj"], "license": "CC BY 4.0 (datameet/maps README default)", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200 (17 MB, all-India states). Field ST_NM; filter ST_NM == \"Goa\". A simpler option is to dissolve the HT goa_district.json into one polygon (the bbox above comes from it)."}, {"what": "PC boundaries (Goa): DO NOT USE for current PCs", "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HindustanTimesLabs/shapefiles/master/state_ut/goa/parliament/goa_PC.json", "license": "MIT (repository licence)", "notes": "Checked: HTTP 200, 2 features, but PC_NAME is \"Panaji\"/\"Mormugao\" (pre-2008 names; now North Goa/South Goa) and the PARTY attributes are stale. Pre-delimitation. Build current PCs by dissolving the AC layer on PC_NO instead."}]}